---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /legal/
title: Legal, Privacy & Compliance
description: Privacy, telehealth, self-pay, prescribing, emergency care, and website-use information for Premier Wellness Telehealth.
---
<main id="main">
  <header class="page-banner">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal, Privacy &amp; Compliance</div>
      <h1>Your privacy. Your care. Our <em>commitment</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        {{ site.name }} is committed to providing professional, secure, and
        transparent virtual healthcare. This page explains important information
        about privacy, telehealth services, payment, prescribing, emergency care,
        and use of this website.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  {% include "partials/wave-divider.njk" %}

  <section class="legal-hub">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal-intro">
        Please review the applicable policies before receiving care. Each policy
        below links to the complete document; this page is an overview, not the
        policy itself.
      </div>

      <section class="legal-section" id="privacy">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 01</span>Privacy &amp; Protected Health Information</h2>
        <p>
          {{ site.name }} respects the privacy of your health information and uses
          safeguards designed to protect information handled in connection with your
          care. Medical information should be submitted only through the secure
          systems and communication methods designated by the practice.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Do not submit sensitive medical information through public website fields unless the form is specifically identified as a secure patient-care form.</li>
          <li>Clinical records, intake information, messages, and other protected health information are handled through the practice's approved healthcare technology and record systems.</li>
          <li>The Notice of Privacy Practices explains how protected health information may be used and disclosed and describes applicable patient rights.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/legal/hipaa/" class="btn btn-outline">View Notice of Privacy Practices</a>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="telehealth">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 02</span>Telehealth Services &amp; Consent</h2>
        <p>
          {{ site.name }} provides virtual healthcare to eligible adult patients who
          are physically located in a state where the treating provider is authorized
          to practice at the time care is delivered. Telehealth may include scheduled
          video visits and, for selected conditions, asynchronous online visits.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Telehealth is not appropriate for every medical concern.</li>
          <li>A provider may recommend an in-person examination, laboratory or diagnostic testing, specialist evaluation, urgent care, or emergency care when clinically appropriate.</li>
          <li>Patients may be required to verify their identity and physical location at the time of care.</li>
          <li>Online visits require completion of requested clinical information. Submission of a questionnaire does not guarantee treatment, a diagnosis, or a prescription.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="self-pay">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 03</span>Self-Pay Services &amp; Financial Responsibility</h2>
        <p>
          {{ site.name }} operates as a self-pay practice. Fees are displayed before
          booking, and patients are responsible for charges associated with the
          services they select.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>{{ site.name }} does not bill health insurance for routine self-pay services.</li>
          <li>Insurance coverage or reimbursement, if independently sought by a patient, is determined by the patient's health plan.</li>
          <li>Laboratory testing, imaging, pharmacy charges, medications, or outside services may involve separate fees unless specifically stated as included.</li>
          <li>{{ derived.cancellationPolicy }}</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/pricing/" class="btn btn-outline">View Pricing</a>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="prescriptions">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 04</span>Prescriptions &amp; Medication Management</h2>
        <p>
          Medication may be prescribed, continued, adjusted, or declined based on the
          provider's clinical judgment, applicable law, patient safety, and the
          information available during the evaluation.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>An appointment or online visit does not guarantee that a medication will be prescribed.</li>
          <li>Some medications or medical conditions may require an in-person examination, laboratory monitoring, prior medical records, or specialty care.</li>
          <li>{{ site.name }} cannot guarantee pharmacy inventory, medication availability, insurance coverage, formulary approval, or pharmacy fulfillment.</li>
          <li>The practice does not prescribe medications that fall outside its clinical scope or prescribing policies. Controlled substances are not prescribed.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="weight-management">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 05</span>Medical Weight Management</h2>
        <p>
          {{ site.name }} offers evidence-based medical management of overweight and
          obesity as one component of comprehensive adult healthcare. The practice is
          not a rapid-weight-loss or medication-dispensing clinic.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Treatment is individualized and based on medical history, clinical assessment, treatment goals, risks, and appropriate monitoring.</li>
          <li>Prescription therapy, including GLP-1 or dual GIP/GLP-1 medications, may be considered when clinically appropriate.</li>
          <li>Booking a consultation does not guarantee eligibility for a particular medication.</li>
          <li>Medication availability, insurance coverage, prior authorization decisions, and pharmacy fulfillment are not guaranteed.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="emergencies">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 06</span>Emergencies &amp; Urgent Medical Needs</h2>
        <div class="emergency-banner">
          <strong>Emergency notice</strong>
          {{ site.name }} does not provide emergency medical services. If you are
          experiencing a medical emergency or potentially life-threatening symptoms,
          call 911 or go to the nearest emergency department. Do not use the website,
          patient portal, messaging system, or an online visit to seek emergency care.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="disclaimer">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 07</span>Website Information &amp; Medical Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          Information provided on this website is for general educational and
          informational purposes and is not a substitute for individualized medical
          evaluation, diagnosis, or treatment. Viewing the website, submitting a
          general inquiry, or reading educational content does not by itself establish
          a provider-patient relationship.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Medical decisions should be based on an appropriate clinical evaluation.</li>
          <li>Do not delay seeking professional or emergency medical care because of information found on this website.</li>
          <li>Website content may be updated as clinical services, laws, technology, or practice policies change.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="accessibility">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 08</span>Accessibility &amp; Nondiscrimination</h2>
        <p>
          {{ site.name }} is committed to respectful and accessible care. If you need
          reasonable communication assistance, or have difficulty accessing website
          content or virtual-care services, please contact us and we will help.
        </p>
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="btn btn-outline">Contact Us for Assistance</a>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="documents">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 09</span>Policies &amp; Important Documents</h2>
        <p>Policies marked as in preparation are being drafted and reviewed before publication.</p>
        <div class="policy-grid">
          {%- for policy in policies %}
          {%- if policy.url %}
          <a href="{{ policy.url }}" class="policy-card">
            <span class="title">{{ policy.title }}</span>
            <span class="status status--available">Available</span>
          </a>
          {%- else %}
          <div class="policy-card policy-card--pending">
            <span class="title">{{ policy.title }}</span>
            <span class="status status--pending">In preparation</span>
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section" id="contact">
        <h2><span class="num">Section 10</span>Contact Information</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these policies may be directed to
          <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
          Office hours are {{ derived.hoursLong }}.
        </p>
        {% if site.mailingAddress %}
        <p>{{ site.mailingAddress }}</p>
        {% endif %}
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
